WEBVTT

00:17.800 --> 00:22.181
The final spotlight fades across the empty

00:22.321 --> 00:27.643
arena floor The road cases are latched and

00:27.743 --> 00:33.765
rolled outside the stage door For twenty years

00:33.845 --> 00:40.267
we gave the world the thunder in our chest Now the

00:40.367 --> 00:46.169
highway's calling us to finally take our rest

00:47.172 --> 00:52.294
Our custom low-floor shuttle bus Is kneeling at

00:52.334 --> 00:59.056
the curb Leading to a quiet place The static

00:59.236 --> 01:05.338
can't disturb Aluminum ramp unfolds beneath

01:05.398 --> 01:12.100
the amber sign Five of us together At the end of

01:12.180 --> 01:19.930
the line We're taking the last bus home Back to

01:20.010 --> 01:26.273
Progress Street Turning off the amplifiers And

01:26.293 --> 01:32.335
the stadium heat Lock the front door tight and

01:32.375 --> 01:35.477
let the curtains fall We don't owe the outside

01:35.517 --> 01:38.839
world anything at all Through every storm we

01:38.879 --> 01:42.301
weathered and every song we played This family

01:42.381 --> 01:48.544
is the greatest music that we ever made

01:52.806 --> 01:57.289
Unplug the synthesizers, set the guitars in

01:57.309 --> 02:02.998
their stands Rest the tired voices and the

02:03.058 --> 02:09.119
callous staking hands Five pairs of sneakers

02:09.539 --> 02:13.940
lined up by the wooden stairs Trade in all the

02:14.000 --> 02:19.221
crowded rooms for quiet living room chairs

02:20.481 --> 02:25.453
We're not fading into nothing We're just tuning

02:25.633 --> 02:29.815
out the noise Back to three sisters and brothers

02:30.415 --> 02:36.038
And the twin ride boys We're taking the last bus

02:36.098 --> 02:42.641
home Back to Progress Street Turning off the

02:42.661 --> 02:49.837
amplifiers And the stadium heat Lock the front

02:49.937 --> 02:52.819
door tight and let the curtains fall We don't

02:52.839 --> 02:56.382
know the outside world, anything at all Through

02:56.502 --> 02:59.224
every storm we weathered and every song we

02:59.264 --> 03:03.087
played This family is the greatest music that we

03:03.207 --> 03:05.710
ever made

03:18.141 --> 03:22.402
Someday when we're ready We'll turn the

03:22.422 --> 03:28.883
switches on And find out that the fire In the

03:29.023 --> 03:32.784
engine's never gone But tonight the porch

03:33.024 --> 03:40.045
light's turning off In Blacksburg town As we lay

03:40.105 --> 03:47.507
the heavy burden Of the road right down

03:53.189 --> 04:14.208
We're

04:14.248 --> 04:20.008
taking the last bus home Back to Progress Street

04:21.309 --> 04:28.555
Turning off the amplifiers And the stadium heat

04:28.615 --> 04:31.437
Lock the front door tight and let the curtains

04:31.497 --> 04:35.020
fall We don't owe the outside world anything at

04:35.060 --> 04:38.022
all Through every storm we weather and every

04:38.082 --> 04:43.527
song we play This family is the greatest music

04:43.827 --> 04:45.168
That we ever made

04:49.872 --> 04:53.602
Lights out on Progress Street Goodnight,

04:55.086 --> 04:56.851
fortunation

